# Knowledge Hub — local configuration template.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. It is the only place machine-specific paths live.
# Every value here is optional; the app falls back to the documented default.
# Reference: docs/06-storage-layout.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KB_DATA_DIR — where the vault lives (SQLite index + every uploaded file).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default when unset:
#   development         ->  <project>/data
#   packaged, installed ->  the OS per-user app data folder
#                           Windows  %APPDATA%\Knowledge Hub\data
#                           macOS    ~/Library/Application Support/Knowledge Hub/data
#                           Linux    ~/.config/Knowledge Hub/data
#   packaged, portable  ->  <folder containing the executable>/data
#                           (opt in by placing a `portable.txt` beside the exe)
#
# RECOMMENDED on this machine: put the vault on the D: drive. C: has ~15 GB
# free, D: has ~212 GB, and the vault is the only part of this project that
# grows without bound (PDFs and Word documents). Source code and node_modules
# stay on the Linux filesystem, which is far faster than a /mnt/* mount.
#
# The app creates the directory on first run if it does not exist.
#
# WSL (Linux path):
# KB_DATA_DIR=/mnt/d/KnowledgeHub
#
# Windows (native, if you ever run the packaged build outside WSL):
# KB_DATA_DIR=D:\KnowledgeHub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KB_DEV_SERVER_URL — renderer origin loaded in development.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Must match the port in `npm run dev:renderer`. Ignored in packaged builds,
# which always load from the app:// protocol.
# KB_DEV_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:3100

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KB_LOG_LEVEL — error | warn | info | debug
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KB_LOG_LEVEL=info
